 ## Overview
-Speedlines are an illustrative visualization technique used to indicate the motion and history of specific features within time-varying datasets [S1, unofficial]. Unlike standard stream lines that trace particle trajectories through a vector field, speedlines superimpose geometric primitives (cones) along the receding bounding contour of a moving feature to provide intuitive visual cues of direction and velocity history [S1, unofficial].
+Speedlines are an illustrative visualization technique used to indicate the motion and history of specific features within time-varying datasets [S1, unofficial]. Unlike standard stream lines that trace particle trajectories through a continuous vector field, speedlines superimpose geometric primitives (cones) along the receding bounding contour of a moving feature to provide intuitive visual cues of direction and velocity history [S1, unofficial].
 
